              <span class="text-rose-500 font-bold text-base shrink-0 mt-0.5">⚠️</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Booking a venue with a hidden food and beverage minimum.</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">Always check whether venue hire requires an obligatory in-house caterer with minimum spend rules.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-rose-50/50 border border-rose-100 p-4 rounded-2xl flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-rose-500 font-bold text-base shrink-0 mt-0.5">⚠️</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Skipping the contingency buffer to afford a bigger guest list.</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">Spending your $700 buffer upfront almost guarantees out-of-pocket credit card balances the week of the event.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-rose-50/50 border border-rose-100 p-4 rounded-2xl flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-rose-500 font-bold text-base shrink-0 mt-0.5">⚠️</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Choosing plated service without pricing buffet first.</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">Plated courses require extra servers, bussers, dish rentals, and kitchen staging fees that balloon quickly.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-rose-50/50 border border-rose-100 p-4 rounded-2xl flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-rose-500 font-bold text-base shrink-0 mt-0.5">⚠️</span>
